So in this question we had to move the array elments to the right by k places.
I have done a question similar to this where we have to check if a sorted array is moved by k places .
I just moved the array index by k places but we get a problem here one problem is that for some indexes it will go out of the array bound.
To fix that I used (k+i)%(no of elements  in the  array)  by this they get placed to there correct place from the start of the array.
Another problem that came was I was overwriting the elements from the original array because of that I was getting false values .
To fix that I made a copy of og array and then changed value in it for every iteration and then changes the og array value to it in the end.

code---
class Solution {
public:
    void rotate(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        vector <int> v = nums;
        for(int i = 0; i<nums.size();i++){
                v[(k+i)%(nums.size())] = nums[i];
        }
        nums = v;
    }
};
Time complexity---
O(n) for copying nums into v
O(n) for for loop 
O(n) for copying 
total time complexity === O(n)

